            <ArticleTitle>Custom database development and biomarker discovery methods for MALDI-TOF mass spectrometry-based identification of high-consequence bacterial pathogens.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>54-57</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0167-7012(17)30019-2</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.mimet.2017.01.009</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A high-quality custom database of MALDI-TOF mass spectral profiles was developed with the goal of improving clinical diagnostic identification of high-consequence bacterial pathogens. A biomarker discovery method is presented for identifying and evaluating MALDI-TOF MS spectra to potentially differentiate biothreat bacteria from less-pathogenic near-neighbour species.</AbstractText>
